{"name": "Postosuchus", "clade": "rauisuchidae", "isd": false, "isnote": "", "sum": "Postosuchus is a large rauisuchid predator of the Late Triassic of North America, named for the Post Quarry in Texas.", "wsnote": "Estimated at 5-6 m long or more (Wikipedia).", "holotype": "Not stated in the sources consulted for this draft; P. kirkpatricki was named by Chatterjee in 1985 from the Post Quarry, Texas.", "material": "Numerous fossils of P. kirkpatricki from the Post Quarry plus remains of P. alisonae from North Carolina; the postcranial skeleton was described by Weinbaum in 2013.", "completeness": "multiple", "exceptional": "", "biology": "It likely preyed on large herbivores such as dicynodonts and on small early dinosaurs; short forelimbs relative to the hind limbs suggest it may have been mainly bipedal.", "author": "Chatterjee 1985", "fad": 237, "lad": 201.4, "early": "Carnian", "late": "Rhaetian", "type_species": "Postosuchus kirkpatricki", "pbdb_occ": 31, "species": [{"name": "Postosuchus alisonae", "author": "Peyer et al. 2008", "fad": 237, "lad": 205.7, "interval": "Carnian–Norian", "ref": ""}, {"name": "Postosuchus kirkpatricki", "author": "Chatterjee 1985", "fad": 227.3, "lad": 205.7, "interval": "Norian", "ref": "original description"}], "formations": [{"ids": ["chinle-united-states"], "formation": "Chinle", "group": "", "members": ["Blue Mesa", "Mesa Redondo", "Owl Rock", "Petrified Forest", "Sonsela"], "country": "United States", "regions": ["Arizona", "New Mexico"], "interval": "Norian–Rhaetian", "n": 21, "ma": [201.4, 227.3]}, {"ids": ["tecovas-united-states"], "formation": "Tecovas", "group": "Dockum", "members": [], "country": "United States", "regions": ["Texas"], "interval": "Carnian–Norian", "n": 4, "ma": [205.7, 237.0]}, {"ids": ["cooper-canyon-united-states"], "formation": "Cooper Canyon", "group": "Dockum", "members": [], "country": "United States", "regions": ["Texas"], "interval": "Norian", "n": 2, "ma": [205.7, 227.3]}, {"ids": ["colorado-ci